WEBVTT

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.200
It's a cheap apartment without a bath,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.700
but we need to at least look 
good on our first day.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.120
We're high school students as of today.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.520
Koori is in middle school.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.110
That's true.

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.340
All right, let's do this!

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.850
Yeah!

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.760
That was a deep sigh, Mana.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.260
If you sigh, your happiness escapes.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.430
Thinking about the three Origami sisters?

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.510
Yeah.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.320
I'm gonna be friends with 
Akara-chin and her sisters!

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.060
That's what I wanted to do, anyway,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.620
but I don't know when I'll see them again.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.050
Cheer up.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.720
I'll share this curry bread with you.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:00:59.450
Yay!

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:02.580
Huh?

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:07.920
Don't worry.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.900
They say yesterday's enemies 
are today's friends.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:11.960
Yeah.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.170
Our enemy is Morgana.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.590
We're all after the same person,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.030
and we're all on the side of good, 
so we'll see each other again.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.520
So...

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:29.300
This is Origami Akara-san. She'll be 
studying with us, starting today.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.830
<b>Origami Akara</b>

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.650
Everyone, get along with her.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.650
<b>Origami 
Hina</b>

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.570
<b>Origami Koori</b>

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.830
Help her figure out 
anything she doesn't know.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.520
Nice to meet y—

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:42.280
I found you again!

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.320
I really found you again!

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.610
<b>Youth! The Crimson Duel</b>

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.560
Morgana...

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:37.700
That dream...

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.890
We're back.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:40.980
We're back.

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.930
Welcome back.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.160
Oh, it's Tsubame-chin!

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.620
What's up? You're in a good mood.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.580
Something good happened.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.040
Something good?

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.500
Akara-san came to school?

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.800
Yeah! She did!

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.440
They're in different years,

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:05.720
but Hina-san and Koori-chan 
both transferred in, too.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.260
I tried hard!

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.600
Tierra-sensei!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.390
Call me Odagiri.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:13.600
I'm surprised they came to school.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.780
It's possible that, somewhere 
deep in their hearts,

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:20.080
those three want to have a normal life.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:21.860
I see.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.320
It was a huge surprise.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.720
I'm going to show them 
around the school tomorrow.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.710
I'll teach them a bunch of stuff.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.330
Wow, you made that agreement with them, huh?

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.670
No, I didn't.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:40.760
I don't know if Akara-san 
will just listen to you.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:43.010
I know!

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:47.380
How about we have Tsubame-chan 
transfer into Goryoukan Academy, too?

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:47.930
Huh?

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.070
Oh, that's a good idea!

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:53.050
If transferring in off-season 
would be embarrassing for you,

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.530
this is your chance!

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.520
You'll have lots of friends!

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:00.840
Yeah.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.030
That might be fun.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.230
Yeah, be optimistic and consider it!

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:10.520
I'll show you around the school.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:12.950
But first, you need to show Akara-san around.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:20.230
Akara-chin, we're moving classes.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.550
The music room is that way.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:24.650
No, it's obviously that way.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:25.170
Huh?

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:27.630
I messed up.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:30.510
There!

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.310
This is really good!

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:40.310
There's a rumor that Hanako of 
the Toilet appears in this stall!

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:46.460
Akara-chin, I'll show you 
the clubs during lunch!

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.280
That's enough! You're annoying me!

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:52.200
Here!

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.260
Here!

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.000
Here!

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.730
Io-chin, you're so cool!

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:58.920
Yo, ace!

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:11.350
I'm so tired.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.310
Akara-chin!

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.600
She's here again.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.190
Hey, guys.

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:18.780
How were classes?

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.030
Think you can keep up?

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:21.770
More like she kept up with me.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:24.050
Sorry about that.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.990
Sorry, but I won't put up with this any longer.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:29.610
I'm going home.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.660
Then, Akara-chin, how about 
we go home together?

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:33.710
That's a good idea.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.080
Want to go bowling?

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.140
Oh, that's something classmates would do!

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.760
I don't have time for that.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.380
I don't have the money for it, either!

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.720
We sisters have to live on our own.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:49.740
I don't want my growing sisters 
to have to go hungry.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:51.590
That's why I need to earn more money,

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:54.600
and at least be able to put some 
extra ingredients in the miso soup!

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.600
In other words, you're looking 
for a part-time job?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.730
In that case, I'll search with you!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:02.190
Huh?

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:03.620
That's a good idea!

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.920
We can't just let her sisters go hungry.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.450
I heard everything you just said.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:14.370
I know of a good position for you.

00:07:17.390 --> 00:07:19.000
So that's what's going on.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.360
Huh? What's that about?

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:26.340
Altair Torte is amazing. That's the point.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.090
They're already friends with Akara-san.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.970
That's Io-senpai for you!

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:35.080
She's the sports star we 
should all strive to be!

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:38.100
Yaginuma Io!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.030
Haruka...

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.810
Oops, you stepped on a landmine.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:45.330
But it's good to make more friends.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:48.450
We should get closer to Hina-san, too.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.610
We're not against each other anymore.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:53.330
Oh, that's youth for you!

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:55.860
Who cares about that?

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:00.620
What's important is that we suffered
a humiliating loss to them!

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:02.490
A black spot on our history!

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:03.870
That still bothers you?

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.540
That's Amane for you.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:10.450
Watch me, Three Origami Sisters.

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:16.150
You're like bugs flying into the flame, 
coming into Goryoukan Academy like that!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.350
Oh, welcome.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.640
Welcome...

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.020
It's so quiet.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:44.560
Was it always this quiet?

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:49.040
Boss, have I changed?

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.870
I didn't know what to do,

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:57.380
but now I think I want to 
go to school with everyone.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:01.810
It might not be that different 
from the life I have right now,

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.610
but I think it'd be fun.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.670
How dare you...

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:11.630
How dare you...

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.670
Morgana!

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.140
That wasn't a dream...

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.840
Those were my memories.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:37.600
I came from that world.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.000
Um, this is...

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.490
They said you can have it.

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.890
Momokawa-san is treating you.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:57.700
Wow!

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:00.050
Is that okay? You're working here.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:02.080
Think of it as a way to say, "Nice to meet you."

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:03.390
Sasa's from a rich family, too.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.530
And you're still working?

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:06.450
Um...

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.260
Forgive me for asking,

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.970
but is this restaurant still 
accepting new employees?

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.610
Could you hire Akara-chan?

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:15.230
What?

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.310
So this is what you meant by "a position"?

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:18.860
Yep!

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.490
We always come here, too.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.760
I see!

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.830
Hey! Don't just decide that for me!

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:29.130
I appreciate that you want to help,

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.670
but I want to find my own place to work.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.570
Later.

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:34.540
A-Akara-chin!

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.540
No good, huh...

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.080
Wait a second.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:41.680
You just completely ignored me, didn't you?

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:46.910
Oh, you're the team I 
accidentally defeated, right?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:49.520
Sorry about that. I wasn't 
really paying attention.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.010
Accidentally? Wasn't paying attention?

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:53.820
Amane...

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.440
I won't let that slide!

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:59.680
Origami Akara, spend the 
rest of the day with us!

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.360
I'm going to pay you back for that.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:05.250
Sorry, but I don't have time to play around—

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.340
Then I'll pay you for the day.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:11.120
Momokawa Sasa, give them ten bags of rice.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.000
Got it.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.390
Wow...

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:17.410
She's just going to pay her on the spot, huh?

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.110
No fair, Amane-chin!

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:20.380
Ama-no-fair-chin!

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:23.430
I'll do whatever I have to.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:26.240
Very well.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:26.760
Huh?!

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.010
I get ten bags of rice if 
I spend time with you.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:30.640
No going back on that?

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:32.100
Of course not.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.110
How do you plan to settle things?

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:36.110
That's a foolish question, Mano.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:38.440
We're Fifth Force.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.620
There's only one way to settle things.

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.280
<b>Currently Out: Tierra</b>

00:12:57.320 --> 00:12:59.240
Will you be okay by yourself?

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:01.530
I can handle a little game like this on my own.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.550
Then I'll go by myself, too.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:04.470
What?

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.540
Amane...

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:08.450
We're fighting one-on-one, got that?

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:11.250
Whoever defeats the most O'bli wins.

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:12.100
Very well.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:14.450
So this is happening again.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:15.990
Do we need to be here?

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:19.010
I guess we're supposed to be witnesses.

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:21.430
We're going to cheer Akara-chin on!

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:25.600
But I've gotten closer to 
Amane-chin lately, too...

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:28.990
Both of you, good luck!

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:30.810
Let's do it!

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:35.720
You're ready, right?

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:36.830
Let's go!

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.630
It's on!

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:41.960
Hold on a second!

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.420
Tsubame-chan!

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.420
Tsubame-san!

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:43.420
Tsubame-chin!

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:48.010
What are you doing using the 
simulation room without permission?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:49.070
Uh...

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:50.300
Well...

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.470
Get out the way! My pride 
is on the line in this battle!

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:56.310
You're being too dramatic.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.560
Were you that frustrated to be 
defeated so quickly by us?

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:03.230
We weren't beaten that badly!

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:06.110
She's getting sucked right into her pace.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.570
They're kind of alike, huh?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.940
Okay, just calm down for a second.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:20.000
Here they come.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:22.180
I'm going to take all of you out!

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:22.890
Hey!

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.390
That's my line!

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:24.960
Wait!

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:29.680
I got one.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.850
I got two.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.430
Four... Five...

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:39.440
Six... Seven...

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.560
They're about even right now.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.660
They're both strong.

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:46.730
I don't know if a mock battle 
is going to settle this.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:47.650
Huh?

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:48.810
Look!

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.880
W-Wait! What's up with that number?

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.570
Did the settings change?

00:14:55.570 --> 00:14:58.290
Well, I thought it'd be more fun this way.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.540
They all have the same face... It's so creepy.

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:06.050
Wait, there aren't supposed to be that many!

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:08.720
Oh, no!

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.930
Now I'm in the lead.

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:15.100
I'll turn that around right now.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:28.360
Hey! Be careful!

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.360
That was a nice punch.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:32.860
Same to you.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:49.720
You're pretty good.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:50.800
You, too.

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.300
Uh...

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.610
Just what is going on?

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:02.440
What?

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:10.900
Something that logic can't explain 
is blooming between those two.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.490
Wh-What should I do?

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.200
I'm crying now, too.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.130
This is youth!

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:20.380
Haruka, I think I understand 
what you were saying!

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:23.460
There are things you can't buy with money.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:29.810
You fight and clash, but then join fists,
and there's something waiting beyond that!

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.840
You can't be honest with yourself.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:34.460
But you're still forced to admit it.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:37.220
Yes, I'm deeply moved.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:39.300
That's youth!

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.100
That's friendship!

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.730
Let's begin!

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:45.690
What is this?

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:53.200
Everyone, what are you doing?

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.880
T-Tierra-sensei...

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:01.540
It's against the rules to use the simulation 
room without permission, moshu.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:08.280
And what were you thinking, 
doing this without asking me first?

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:16.340
Why do I have to do this, too?

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:19.300
I shouldn't be working here for free.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.400
I'm going to make Hina 
and Koori go hungry again.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.680
Um...

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.770
This is your payment for today, as promised.

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:30.240
Also...

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:31.980
Take this, too.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.280
It's a bit lonely to have only rice.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.140
Huh?

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:36.980
Akara-san, you can go.

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:38.610
We'll be done soon, anyway.

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:40.300
Sorry we got you involved in this.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:43.010
Your sisters might be worried.

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:45.460
Yeah, let us take care of the rest.

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:48.220
Th-Thanks.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.680
I'll give you a discount.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:54.960
I had a lot of fun.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.290
I'll take this, though.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:58.540
Bye.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:02.030
Akara-san's a pretty good girl.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:02.600
Yeah.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.890
That's right! She is!

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.350
Akara-chin is a really good girl!

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:10.100
I'm not sure about that.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.480
You just can't be honest with 
yourself, huh, Leader?

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:15.710
Sh-Shut up!

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.530
Tsubame-chan.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.700
We're sorry.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.210
You only came to stop us,

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.120
but you ended up being lectured, too.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:33.200
We caused trouble for our leader.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.860
You can have this curry bread as an apology.

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:37.510
Sorry, Tsubame-chin.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.220
T-Tsubame-chan?

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:52.530
Did you get hurt?

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:53.230
No.

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:56.180
Th-There was something my eye.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:56.820
Sorry.

00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:58.500
What? Are you okay?

00:18:58.500 --> 00:18:59.650
Does it hurt?

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.020
I'm fine.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:03.780
I'm going to wash my face, 
so go ahead without me.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:20.910
Your memories came back?

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.260
What should I do?

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:25.630
Should I tell everyone?

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:30.100
In the world I was in, 
the O'bli got everyone...

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:34.080
I wish I han't remembered anything.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.500
That's interesting.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:35.980
Huh?

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:38.660
Worlds separate from this one,

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:42.800
which we call parallel worlds, do exist.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:47.120
The Memoca borrow powers from 
your selves in other parallel worlds,

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:49.340
and are then used for combat.

00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:53.880
Theoretically, in the infinite parallel worlds,

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:56.910
there should be the same number of "yous."

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:03.320
Yes, if you are the Miyama-san 
that came from another world,

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:07.430
where did the you from this world go?

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.100
Were you never here?

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.100
If that's the case, Miyama-san,

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.520
you might be someone special.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:21.120
An important key in the fight against Morgana.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:25.070
So you did flee to this dimension.

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:28.860
I don't know.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.020
But I don't want to see anything 
from that dream again.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:36.380
I won't let anything happen 
to hurt my friends.

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:38.160
It'll be fine.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:43.820
It might have been tough for you,
getting your memories back,

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:47.600
but you've become stronger because of it.

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:49.720
So it'll be fine.

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:54.140
No matter the trouble, 
you'll be able to get through it

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:56.270
with your friends.

00:20:58.660 --> 00:20:59.650
I'm back.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:00.660
Tsubame-chin!

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:01.660
Welcome back.

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:04.350
Now that everyone's here, it's time for dinner.

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:05.990
How many curry breads have you eaten?

00:21:08.980 --> 00:21:12.020
Once you decide, we can do it anytime.

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.500
Everyone's waiting.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.460
Oh, it's Boss.

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:18.380
He came to see you.

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:20.990
Boss likes you the best.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:22.170
You think so?

00:21:23.040 --> 00:21:25.050
Hey, Boss.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:28.550
You know, that's a weird name, 
now that I think about it.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:31.680
Yeah, I guess it is. And we never 
know when he'll show up.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:35.920
Moshune-chan took Boss in.

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:39.310
It was when Fifth Force was 
just formed, apparently.

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.440
Huh...

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:42.330
I see.

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:45.080
Just like me.

00:23:20.300 --> 00:23:23.080
White rice, and miso soup with green onion.

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:25.260
This is really fancy!

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:27.650
Did something good happen, Onee?

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:29.440
Yeah, I suppose so.

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:31.300
Now, then...

00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:33.340
Let's eat.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Arrived! The Lone Knight</b>

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:40.980
"Arrived! The Lone Knight."
